WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.230
Meet EME.

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.850
The Editing Mechanics Engine.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.960
A local video studio that connects your creative intent

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.400
to precise, reviewable edits.

00:00:11.083 --> 00:00:12.363
Bring in your footage.

00:00:12.363 --> 00:00:15.003
Shape the story on a multi-track timeline.

00:00:15.003 --> 00:00:18.463
Trim and split clips, keep audio linked, and fine-tune

00:00:18.493 --> 00:00:20.393
every detail in the inspector.

00:00:22.113 --> 00:00:25.493
Or describe the change to your connected IDE agent.

00:00:25.493 --> 00:00:27.843
It proposes a plan through MCP.

00:00:27.843 --> 00:00:30.523
You review the exact edit, then approve it.

00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:33.777
Build a visual language.

00:00:33.777 --> 00:00:37.567
Compare editorial, balanced, and energetic designs.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:41.117
Titles, lower thirds, and statistic cards, with measured

00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:43.167
typography and composed motion.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.410
Then deliver with evidence.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.350
EME renders the committed edit and checks the final

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.380
video, audio, fonts, and protected-title placement before

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.870
publishing the export.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:58.430
Your agent brings the ideas.

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.240
You keep creative control.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.370
EME.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.300
From intent, to edit, to evidence.
